    LLM: 'Game: Kierki. See rules.objective and rules.gameplay for details.',
    Player: 'Kierki (Polish Hearts) is the Polish variant of the classic avoidance trick-taking game Hearts. Played by four players, it features a unique multi-hand structure where the objective changes each roundâ€”from avoiding hearts to avoiding queens, or taking no tricks at all. It is a game of high strategic depth and defensive maneuvering.',
    objective: 'Avoid taking specific penalty cards or tricks across a series of rounds.',
    gameplay: '1. Standard trick-taking. Must follow suit.\n2. No trumps are used in most Kierki variants.\n3. The leading player can lead any card (except Hearts in the first trick of the Hearts hand).',
